Paragraph text:
Backbone Models & Datasets. We deploy three lightweight open-source LLMs; Llama3.2(3B) (Ol- lama, 2024b), Mistral(7B) (AI, 2023) and Qwen2.5(7B) (Yang et al., 2024) as both agents use of the Credibility Scoring mechanism, and the accuracy gain over naive coordination is denoted by ∆. Backbone Model Architecture GSM8K MMLU-MS MATH Research QA CrS ∆ CrS ∆ CrS ∆ CrS ∆ LLaMA 3.2(3B)SIA 47.5 +8% 35.5 +15% 40.0 +7% 52.0 +51% CrS-ordered Chain 43.0 +20% 44.0 +16% 32.0 +15% 84.0 +20% Mistral(7B)SIA 12.0 +6% 21.0 +9% 11.5 +5.5% 86.0 +14% CrS-ordered Chain 13.0 +11% 32.0 +6% 08.0 +6% 77.0 −7% Qwen2.5(7B)SIA 75.5 +10.5% 43.0 +25.5% 65.0 - 59.0 +17% CrS-ordered Chain 60.0 +10% 52.0 +10% 59.8 +9% 90.0 +5% and coordinator, allowing cost-efficient scaling while testing models that remain susceptible to adversarial noise. A stronger GPT-4o mini (Ol- lama, 2024a) acts as an external judge, evaluating and scoring the team’s final answers. We evaluated our framework on five benchmarks: MMLU-MS(Hendrycks et al., 2020) (Math and Statistics),MATH (Hendrycks et al., 2021), GSM8K (Cobbeet al., 2021)(open-ended mathematical reasoning), HumanEval (Chen et al., 2021)(code completion), and Research Questions (Rosset et al., 2024)(non -factoid, search -style questions requiringcontextual judgment).

